# Known divergence (by design): make_test_raster's body runs a dynamic EXECUTE, so
# the gateway rejects its CREATE (the single +ERROR line below). make_test_raster
# is defined across ~23 raster test files, but only this file's copy is actually
# rejected, so its calls are renamed per-file to make_test_raster_tickets (by
# patchPostGISConflictingHelpers) and that name is seeded on the primary -- which
# keeps the dependent SELECT calls working without colliding with the 22 other,
# self-created make_test_raster variants ("function is not unique"). The lone
# residual is thus the honest rejection of the test's own CREATE.
